menuconfig STUN
	bool "STUN (Session Traversal Utilities for NAT) library [EXPERIMENTAL]"
	select EXPERIMENTAL
	select PSA_CRYPTO
	select CRC
	select UTF8
	imply PSA_WANT_ALG_HMAC
	imply PSA_WANT_KEY_TYPE_HMAC
	imply PSA_WANT_ALG_SHA_1
	imply PSA_WANT_ALG_SHA_256
	help
	  STUN message codec as defined in RFC 8489: parsing and building of
	  messages, the MESSAGE-INTEGRITY and MESSAGE-INTEGRITY-SHA256
	  attributes (computed through the PSA Crypto API), FINGERPRINT and
	  the attributes ICE (RFC 8445) adds. The library does no I/O.

	  Both integrity attributes need HMAC of the PSA Crypto API,
	  MESSAGE-INTEGRITY with SHA-1 and MESSAGE-INTEGRITY-SHA256 with
	  SHA-256. All of it is enabled by default. The functions that
	  compute or verify an attribute return -EIO if the backend lacks
	  what the attribute needs.

if STUN

module = STUN
module-dep = NET_LOG
module-str = Log level for STUN
module-help = Enable the log of the STUN library.
source "subsys/net/Kconfig.template.log_config.net"

endif # STUN
